                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">While cursed, the target receives 30% reduced healing.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">The curse is slowly lifted over 8s, restoring the lost HP.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">While cursed, the target receives 60% reduced healing.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The only confirmed position-dependent skill in the game: it targets the enemy standing at the mirror position to Wen-Shen's slot on the battlefield. This makes positioning both exploitable and counterplayable. Damage is based on the target's max HP - an anti-tank tool that scales against high-HP enemies regardless of Wen-Shen's own ATK. The heal restoration over time means this is not a finisher; it is a pressure tool. With Relic Lv3 active, every cast permanently Jinxes the target - making this the primary Jinx application in non-death scenarios.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/wenshen_skill_3.webp" alt="Calamity-Ridden" />
                <span class="skill-name">Calamity-Ridden</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Passive</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                <strong>Passive:</strong> The enemy defeating Wen-Shen becomes <span class="doom">permanently Jinxed</span>. Jinxed: 50% chance to be Stunned, Terrified, or Petrified for 2.5s when attacking; 50% chance to be Knocked Down when moving. Jinx can only trigger once every 4s.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Enemies also take DMG equal to 50% of her ATK per sec while Jinxed.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Jinxed enemies deal 20% reduced DMG.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Increases the chance of triggering a Jinxed effect to 60%.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The death passive reframes how Wen-Shen's health is valued in a fight. Killing her is not a clean win for the opposing team - the assassin or carry that eliminates her inherits a permanent CC liability. At Lv3, the 20% damage reduction on Jinxed enemies is particularly impactful: the hero that kills her becomes a weakened version of itself for the rest of the match. This passive makes Wen-Shen a hard counter to glass-cannon assassins who rely on burst to finish her quickly.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/wenshen_skill_4.webp" alt="Cursed Ground" />
                <span class="skill-name">Cursed Ground</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 4</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                <strong>Passive:</strong> Creates an Aura of Misfortune within a 3-meter radius, reducing the <span class="highlight">ATK of enemies inside by 20%</span>.<br/><br/>
                <strong>Active:</strong> Flies toward the enemy with the <span class="highlight">highest ATK</span>, dealing DMG equal to <strong>180% of ATK</strong>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Enemies inside the Aura also have their DEF reduced by 20%.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Increases DMG dealt to 200% ATK.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Wen-Shen's Aura of Misfortune lingers on the spot when she is defeated.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Lv4 is the combination unlock with Calamity-Ridden: when Wen-Shen dies, the Aura of Misfortune remains on the battlefield at her last position, continuing to reduce enemy ATK and DEF. The enemy who killed her is permanently Jinxed. Two post-death effects activate simultaneously. The active component's targeting logic - highest ATK enemy - means it will consistently find the primary carry or DPS unit, applying the debuff aura directly on top of the highest-priority threat.
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Skill Upgrade Priority</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>1. Star of Ill Omen (Ultimate)</strong> - Core lockdown; Lv4 extends hard CC to 6s and maximizes DoT output per cycle</li>
              <li><strong>2. Calamity-Ridden (Skill 3)</strong> - Lv3's 20% damage reduction on Jinxed is a permanent team-wide defensive buff activated by Wen-Shen's death</li>
              <li><strong>3. Origin of Pestilence (Relic)</strong> - Lv3 is a mechanic unlock: Duality Inversion becomes a reliable active Jinx setter; Lv4 adds 20% increased damage taken on all Jinxed targets</li>
              <li><strong>4. Cursed Ground (Skill 4)</strong> - Lv4 aura persistence after death compounds with the death passive; upgrade after core skills are set</li>
              <li><strong>5. Duality Inversion (Skill 2)</strong> - Heal reduction scales with Relic investment; lower standalone priority but unlocks the Jinx chain at Relic Lv3</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RATINGS -->
        <section class="section" id="wenshen-ratings">
          <div class="section-title">Mode Ratings (Theoretical)</div>
          <div class="rating-grid">
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVP</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="SS">SS</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Hard CC Ultimate + permanent death debuff = one of the strongest anti-carry tools in PVP meta</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVE / Campaign</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="S">S</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Heal reduction and ATK debuff aura provide consistent value; Cursed Ground and debuff kit scale well in extended campaign fights</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">Boss Fights</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="B">B</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Duality Inversion's max-HP damage is useful; Jinx CC RNG is less impactful on single targets with high control resistance</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">Tower / Progression</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="A">A</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">ATK/DEF aura debuffs and heal reduction contribute to multi-stage survivability; death passive triggers reliably</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:12px; font-style:italic; text-align:center;">* All ratings theoretical - based on skill mechanics and CN community meta analysis. No global server data available (hero not yet released).</p>
        </section>

        <!-- POSITIONING -->
        <section class="section" id="wenshen-positioning">
          <div class="section-title">Recommended Positioning</div>
          <div class="pos-grid">
            <div class="pos-card">
              <div class="pos-mode">Mid-Frontline - Intentionally Expendable</div>
              <p>Wen-Shen is the only hero in the game who is designed to die on purpose. Her death passive and Skill 4's lingering aura are most valuable when she is eliminated at a point where her team still has fighting capacity to exploit the aftermath. Placing her too far back delays her death and wastes the passive window; placing her in the hard frontline may cause her to die before her Ultimate and Duality Inversion have fired.</p>
              <p>The optimal position is mid-priority - accessible enough that she draws an early elimination attempt, but not so exposed that she falls before contributing her CC and debuffs. Position 2 or 3 is typically correct depending on team composition.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pos-card">
              <div class="pos-mode">Formation Structure</div>
              <p><strong>Front:</strong> A tank or bruiser who absorbs the opening burst and keeps the enemy occupied while Wen-Shen's kit fires.</p>
              <p><strong>Mid (Wen-Shen):</strong> She needs one or two skill casts before dying - her Skill 4 active dash should connect before she falls, placing the Aura of Misfortune on the highest-ATK enemy.</p>
              <p><strong>Back:</strong> Damage carries and support. They are the primary beneficiaries of the Jinx debuff, the ATK/DEF aura, and the heal reduction - they must be alive to collect the value her death generates.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- COMPS -->
        <section class="section" id="wenshen-comps">
          <div class="section-title">Suggested Comps</div>
          <div class="comp-list">
            {guides.find(g => g.id === "wenshen")!.comps.map(comp => (
              <div class="comp-entry">
                <div class="comp-entry-header">
                  <span class="comp-label">{comp.label}</span>
                  <p class="comp-reason">{comp.reason}</p>
