          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Hera is a <strong>Legendary Support</strong> of the <strong>Starglint faction</strong> built around a dual-axis control identity: she simultaneously <em>neutralizes</em> the most dangerous enemy carry and <em>amplifies</em> the friendliest carry. No other support in the current roster does both at once.</p>
            <p>Her Ultimate, <strong>Tide of Obsession</strong>, charms the nearest enemy and forces them to attack their own team - turning the opposing DPS into a liability. Her Skill 2, <strong>Fatal Infatuation</strong>, marks the highest-damage enemy with an Obsession debuff that locks them out of attacking entirely and pulls them toward Hera while dealing DoT. Her Skill 1, <strong>Crown's Bestowal</strong>, simultaneously buffs the friendly hero with the highest ATK with both ATK and ATK Speed.</p>
            <p>Her passive, <strong>Royal Domain</strong>, places a field over the friendly half at battle start. Inside it, Hera regenerates Energy faster and gains stacking damage reduction - making her naturally harder to burst down early, which is critical for a unit whose value comes from completing multiple control cycles.</p>
            <p>The CN community describes her as a <em>stronger, modernized variant of Pan</em> - a control-focused support whose ceiling rises sharply with Relic investment, particularly at Relic Lv3. Official release: 18 February 2026 on CN server.</p>
            <p class="note-muted">All ratings and strategic assessments are based on CN server skill data and early community analysis (TapTap CN). Data current as of March 2026. Numerical stats are not available in this guide.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- LORE -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-lore">
          <div class="section-title">Lore &amp; Background</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Queen of Olympus - Greek Mythology</div>
            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Hera is the queen of the Olympian gods in Greek mythology - goddess of marriage, family, and sovereign power. Wife and sister of Zeus, she is famous for her fierce jealousy, her dominion over the fates of heroes and enemies alike, and her absolute authority over those within her domain. The game draws directly on these themes for her mechanical identity.</p>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><em>Tide of Obsession</em> mirrors Hera's mythological weaponization of madness and desire - she famously drove heroes to ruin by bending their minds against them</li>
              <li><em>Fatal Infatuation</em> reflects her role as the goddess who draws enemies inward and claims them, pulling the threat that poses the greatest danger into her orbit</li>
              <li><em>Crown's Bestowal</em> represents her sovereign authority to crown and elevate - Hera grants her chosen champion the power of a king</li>
              <li><em>Royal Domain</em> embodies her claim over Olympus itself: within her half of the battlefield, her authority is absolute and her power is amplified</li>
              <li>The Relic, <em>Charm Seal</em>, is her brand of ownership - enemies she has controlled bear her mark and are left permanently weakened in their resistance to her</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- CHARM SYSTEM -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-charm-system">
          <div class="section-title">Core Mechanic - The Charm Control Loop</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">How Hera's Control Chain Works</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>Hera has two distinct control states she applies: <span class="highlight">Charm</span> (魅惑) from her Ultimate, and <span class="highlight">Obsession</span> (痴迷) from Fatal Infatuation. Both are covered by her Relic.</li>
              <li><strong>Charm:</strong> The charmed target attacks its own allies. Hera's Ultimate also boosts the charmed target's normal attack damage - making the most powerful auto-attacker on the enemy team the most dangerous weapon pointed at themselves.</li>
              <li><strong>Obsession:</strong> The obsessed target cannot attack at all, moves slower, and is continuously pulled toward Hera. It takes DoT while Hera heals herself for the same amount. This is a hard anti-carry disable, not just a redirection.</li>
              <li><strong>Charm Seal (Relic):</strong> Enemies who have been under either Charm or Obsession lose <span class="highlight">Effect Resistance</span> permanently for the rest of the fight. This makes all subsequent control attempts more reliable.</li>
              <li><strong>Relic Lv3</strong> is the critical breakpoint: charmed enemies can no longer gain Energy. This converts Charm from a simple redirection into <span class="highlight">Control + Energy Denial</span> - the charmed carry cannot build toward their own Ultimate while they fight their teammates.</li>
              <li><strong>Relic Lv4:</strong> If the charmed unit kills an ally during the Charm duration, the Charm is extended. The more dangerous the charmed target, the longer the effect persists.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top:16px; border-color: rgba(180,130,80,0.25); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(180,130,80,0.06), rgba(180,130,80,0.04));">
            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--accent-gold-light);">Internal Kit Synergy</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>Crown's Bestowal</strong> buffs the friendly carry with the highest ATK - while <strong>Fatal Infatuation</strong> simultaneously locks down the opposing carry with the highest damage output. One cast covers both flanks.</li>
              <li><strong>Tide of Obsession</strong> charms a third target and redirects their auto-attacks, creating a three-vector control state: friendly carry boosted, enemy carry locked, second enemy turned on their own team.</li>
              <li><strong>Royal Domain</strong> provides passive Energy regeneration that accelerates Hera's own Ultimate cycle - the longer the fight, the faster she rotates through her control chain.</li>
              <li>Hera's kit does not fight against itself. Each piece reinforces the same goal: protect your carry, neutralize their carry, and convert enemy aggression into self-inflicted damage.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SKILLS -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-skills">
