              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">The charmed target's normal attack damage bonus is increased further.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Charm duration is extended.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">The charmed target's normal attack damage bonus is increased further.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The boosted normal attack damage is the key detail: Hera does not just disable a threat, she amplifies it and redirects it. The stronger the enemy auto-attacker, the more damage their own team absorbs during the Charm duration. Works most devastatingly against teams with a dominant auto-attack carry.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card relic">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/hera_relic.webp" alt="Charm Seal" />
                <span class="skill-name">Charm Seal</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-relic">Relic</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Enemies who have been under Hera's <span class="highlight">Charm</span> or <span class="highlight">Obsession</span> control have their <span class="highlight">Effect Resistance reduced</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Charmed enemies also receive Crown's Bestowal (Hera's own ATK/ATK Speed buff applied to the enemy carry).</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Charmed enemies cannot gain Energy for the duration of the Charm.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">If the charmed enemy kills an ally during the Charm, the Charm duration is extended.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Relic Lv3 is Hera's most important investment threshold. Adding Energy Denial to Charm converts a strong CC effect into a strategic shutdown: the charmed carry cannot build toward their own Ultimate while damaging their allies. Lv4 creates a self-sustaining loop if the charmed unit is strong enough to actually secure kills.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/hera_skill_2.webp" alt="Crown's Bestowal" />
                <span class="skill-name">Crown's Bestowal</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 1</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Hera grants her crown to the friendly hero with the <span class="highlight">highest ATK</span>, increasing their <strong>ATK</strong> and <strong>ATK Speed</strong> for a duration.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">ATK bonus is increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Duration is extended.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">ATK Speed bonus is increased.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Auto-targeting means no manual carry designation is needed: the highest-ATK ally always receives the buff. Build your team's carry to have the highest ATK and the crown reliably lands on the correct target every cycle. The ATK Speed component makes this particularly valuable for heroes whose output scales with attack frequency.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/hera_skill_3.webp" alt="Fatal Infatuation" />
                <span class="skill-name">Fatal Infatuation</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 2</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Targets the enemy dealing the <span class="highlight">highest damage</span> and applies <span class="highlight">Obsession</span>: the target cannot attack, moves slower, and is gradually pulled toward Hera. The target takes DoT equal to a percentage of Hera's ATK per second. Hera heals herself for the same amount.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">DoT per second is increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Obsession duration is extended.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">DoT per second is increased further.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                This is an unconditional hard-disable against the opposing team's most threatening damage source. Unlike Charm, Obsession does not redirect the target - it simply removes them from the fight entirely for its duration while restoring Hera's HP. The combination of immobilization, DoT, and self-healing makes this the most directly impactful skill in her kit on a per-cast basis.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/hera_skill_4.webp" alt="Royal Domain" />
                <span class="skill-name">Royal Domain</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Passive</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                At battle start, Hera deploys a <span class="highlight">Power Field</span> over the friendly half of the battlefield. Inside the field, Hera regenerates Energy faster and gains stacking <strong>Damage Reduction</strong> (up to a cap). When enemies first enter the field, they are <span class="highlight">Suppressed</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Damage reduction inside the field is increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Suppression duration on enemy entry is extended.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">When Hera would take fatal damage, she withdraws the field, becomes briefly immune, and heals a percentage of her Max HP.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Royal Domain is Hera's durability engine. The Energy regeneration bonus accelerates her Ultimate cycle, ensuring she completes multiple Charm rotations in a single fight. The Suppression on enemy entry to the friendly half can interrupt dives and disrupt aggressive engage patterns. Lv4 provides a pseudo-revival identical in concept to Skadi's Relic Lv2 - a last-resort survival window rather than a passive sustain tool.
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Skill Upgrade Priority</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>1. Charm Seal (Relic)</strong> - Lv3 Energy Denial is the most impactful breakpoint in Hera's entire kit; prioritize Relic investment above all else</li>
              <li><strong>2. Fatal Infatuation (Skill 2)</strong> - The hard anti-carry disable; Lv3 duration extension significantly increases the window the opposing carry is removed from the fight</li>
              <li><strong>3. Tide of Obsession (Ultimate)</strong> - More Charm duration and higher redirected damage at higher levels; primary control tool</li>
              <li><strong>4. Royal Domain (Passive)</strong> - Lv4 pseudo-revival is valuable as insurance; Lv3 extended Suppression improves field control</li>
              <li><strong>5. Crown's Bestowal (Skill 1)</strong> - Strong carry buff, but lower priority than the control skills that define Hera's kit</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RATINGS -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-ratings">
          <div class="section-title">Mode Ratings</div>
          <div class="rating-grid">
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVP</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="S">S</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Anti-carry targeting, Charm redirection, Energy Denial via Relic Lv3 - oppressive against single-carry compositions</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVE / Campaign</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="A">A</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Strong carry buff and control provide consistent value; team-dependent in content where enemies resist or ignore CC</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">Tower / Progression</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="A">A</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Control and self-sustain via Royal Domain support extended multi-stage fights; value depends on content's CC susceptibility</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">Boss Fights</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="B">B</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Crown's Bestowal adds carry support value; core CC identity diminished when targets are immune to Charm and Obsession</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p style="font-size:12px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:12px; font-style:italic; text-align:center;">* Ratings based on CN server skill data and early community meta analysis (TapTap CN, March 2026). Exact tier positioning is preliminary - insufficient long-term data available for a hard rating above A in PVE.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- POSITIONING -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-positioning">
          <div class="section-title">Recommended Positioning</div>
          <div class="pos-grid">
            <div class="pos-card">
              <div class="pos-mode">Backline - Control Anchor</div>
              <p>Hera should be placed in a protected backline position. Her Royal Domain automatically covers the friendly half, meaning she benefits from its Energy regeneration and damage reduction regardless of her exact position within it. Her Skill targeting is auto-directed - no manual positioning is required to hit the correct targets.</p>
              <p>Keeping Hera alive through multiple control cycles is the primary constraint. Each subsequent cast of Fatal Infatuation and Tide of Obsession applies the Charm Seal debuff again, reducing Effect Resistance further. More cycles = more reliable control = more value extracted from the Relic investment.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="pos-card">
              <div class="pos-mode">Formation Structure</div>
              <p><strong>Front:</strong> Tank or taunt unit (Momus recommended by CN community) - absorbs initial burst and establishes the first control interaction that Hera compounds on.</p>
              <p><strong>Mid:</strong> Your highest-ATK carry - Crown's Bestowal will target them automatically. Build this hero for ATK to guarantee consistent targeting. Pan or a second CC unit can fill the fourth slot to extend control chains.</p>
              <p><strong>Back:</strong> Hera + healing support. Hera's self-heal from Fatal Infatuation provides partial sustain, but a dedicated healer (Yuelao, Cancer) significantly improves her survival in long fights.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RECOMMENDED COMPS -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-comps">
          <div class="section-title">Suggested Comps</div>
          <div class="comp-list">
            {guides.find(g => g.id === "hera")!.comps.map(comp => (
              <div class="comp-entry">
                <div class="comp-entry-header">
                  <span class="comp-label">{comp.label}</span>
                  <p class="comp-reason">{comp.reason}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-hero-row">
                  {comp.heroes.map(id => (
