                      <div class="hero-card-chip-portrait" aria-hidden="true"></div>
                      <span class="hero-card-chip-name">{heroName(id)}</span>
                    </a>
                  ))}
                </div>
                {comp.notes?.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="comp-notes">
                    {comp.notes.map(n => <li>{n}</li>)}
                  </ul>
                )}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- STRENGTHS / WEAKNESSES -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-strengths">
          <div class="section-title">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses</div>
          <div class="sw-grid">
            <div class="sw-card strengths">
              <div class="sw-title">Strengths</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Dual-axis control: simultaneously buffs friendly carry (Crown's Bestowal) and disables enemy carry (Fatal Infatuation) in the same rotation</li>
                <li>Charm redirection converts the most dangerous enemy auto-attacker into a source of friendly fire - value scales with the strength of the charmed target</li>
                <li>Royal Domain provides passive Energy regeneration, enabling faster Ultimate cycles than most supports without external Energy support</li>
                <li>Charm Seal Relic stacks Effect Resistance reduction after each control event, making all subsequent CC more reliable as the fight progresses</li>
                <li>Relic Lv3 adds Energy Denial to Charm - a hard counter to Ultimate-dependent enemy carries</li>
                <li>Self-heal from Fatal Infatuation provides partial sustain without requiring a dedicated healer slot</li>
                <li>Royal Domain Lv4 pseudo-revival acts as a survival safety net equivalent in concept to Skadi's Relic Lv2</li>
                <li>CN community rates her as a stronger, more modern variant of Pan - indicating high competitive ceiling</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sw-card weaknesses">
              <div class="sw-title">Weaknesses &amp; Counters</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Heavily gated by Relic investment - considered significantly stronger at Relic Lv3 and above; weaker at low investment levels</li>
                <li>Charm and Obsession both fail against high Effect Resistance targets, CC-immune enemies, or Cleanse abilities</li>
                <li>Value drops sharply against multi-carry or balanced teams without a dominant single DPS to disable</li>
                <li>Crown's Bestowal requires the team to have a clear highest-ATK carry to benefit - unfocused team builds dilute the buff</li>
                <li>Boss and PvE content with CC-immune enemies strips most of her kit value, leaving only the carry buff</li>
                <li>Burst compositions that eliminate Hera before she completes a second control cycle prevent the Charm Seal stack from compounding</li>
                <li>Still early meta: exact Relic breakpoints and dupe value remain under-documented (data as of March 2026)</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SYNERGY -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-synergy">
          <div class="section-title">Synergy Considerations</div>
          <div class="synergy-list">
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Momus</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">The CN community's primary recommended partner (source: TapTap, Feb/March 2026). Momus's AoE Taunt creates the first CC state on the frontline, which Hera's Charm then layers on top. The combination leaves the opposing team with no safe attack target: taunted units cannot stop attacking Momus, charmed units attack their own allies. Also functions as the primary tank protecting Hera's backline position.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Hladgunnr (Swan)</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">The natural Crown's Bestowal target in most compositions: high ATK value ensures she reliably receives the buff, and she benefits significantly from both the ATK multiplier and the ATK Speed component. Her burst payloads land into windows that Hera's Charm and Obsession create, where the opposing team is either attacking themselves or locked out of responding.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Pan</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">AoE CC partner that chains directly with Hera's single-target control. Pan's silence and daze extend the windows enemies spend unable to act, compounding with Charm Seal's accumulated Effect Resistance reduction. CN community references a "Hera + Momus" CC chain composition that could equivalently substitute Pan for the AoE CC layer.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Yuelao</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Healing support that covers Hera's partial self-sustain and extends her survivability between control cycles. The CN "san-xiang-dui" (three-item team) composition specifically pairs Hera with Yuelao and Cancer as the healing core. Keeping Hera alive into the third or fourth control rotation extracts the full compounding value of the Charm Seal Effect Resistance reduction.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Caishen</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Team-wide Energy acceleration compounds with Hera's Royal Domain Energy regeneration. More Energy means faster Ultimate rotations, which means faster Charm cycles and more Charm Seal stacks in the same fight window. In sustained compositions, Caishen can create near-constant Ultimate availability across the team.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Mengpo</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Revival stacks directly with Hera's Royal Domain Lv4 pseudo-revival for double insurance. Longer fights compound Hera's Charm Seal stacks further - and Mengpo's Lycoris Bloom may target Hera if she leads in Energy inside her Royal Domain, providing additional ATK% on top of her damage reduction. Recommended for sustained PVE compositions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="divider-ornament">&#10022; &#10022; &#10022;</div>

        <!-- PLAYSTYLE SUMMARY -->
        <section class="section" id="hera-playstyle">
          <div class="section-title">Playstyle Summary</div>
          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Hera plays as a <em>dual-axis control support</em> - a hero whose value comes not from healing, shielding, or raw output, but from simultaneous offensive and defensive manipulation. In the opening phase, Royal Domain is already active: Hera is passively accelerating her Energy regeneration and stacking damage reduction before a single skill fires.</p>
            <p>The core rotation executes simultaneously on both flanks: Crown's Bestowal finds the friendly carry and boosts them; Fatal Infatuation finds the opposing carry and removes them; Tide of Obsession charms a third target and turns their attacks against their own team. In a single rotation, Hera has buffed the most important friendly unit, disabled the most dangerous enemy unit, and created a source of friendly fire within the opposing team.</p>
            <p>The Relic is not optional for competitive play. At Relic Lv1, Hera reduces Effect Resistance on controlled targets - meaningful but not decisive. At Relic Lv3, the charmed carry cannot gain Energy during the Charm window. That changes the role entirely: Hera is no longer just redirecting a threat, she is denying them the resources to respond with their own Ultimate. Each subsequent Charm rotation compounds this advantage through accumulated Charm Seal stacks.</p>
            <p>The critical investment question is Relic Lv3. Below it, Hera is a strong but beatable support. At it, the CN community considers her among the most oppressive control tools in PVP - particularly effective against Isis-centric auto-attack compositions where her Charm creates maximum friendly fire and her Relic blocks the Energy cycle that keeps Isis online.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
    )}

