          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Nine Heavens Mysterious Lady - Chinese Mythology</div>
            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Jiutian Xuannv (九天玄女) is a celestial goddess from Chinese mythology - a divine strategist who advised the Yellow Emperor in his wars against Chi You. She embodies cosmic order, military wisdom, and the principle that a superior strategist reads the entire battlefield before making a single move. The game draws directly on these themes for her mechanical identity.</p>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><em>Win Half Against Heaven</em> (胜天半子) channels her role as the celestial advisor who tips the scales - not by brute force but by reading when to press and when to yield</li>
              <li><em>Swift Control, Slow Response</em> (速御迟) reflects her doctrine of strategic patience: designate your pieces, control the board, and let position determine outcome</li>
              <li><em>Tactical Interception</em> (插制巧) is the art of disrupting the enemy's flow - seizing energy when they are weak and draining it when they are strong</li>
              <li><em>Enter the Game</em> (身入局) embodies her most famous principle: true mastery requires placing oneself within the situation, not outside it - she absorbs the threat and returns it</li>
              <li>The Relic, <em>Strike the Void, Hit the Real</em> (虚击实), is the crown of her strategic philosophy: appear to strike empty air, and land on the real target</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- STANCE SYSTEM -->
        <section class="section" id="jiutian-stance-system">
          <div class="section-title">Core Mechanic - The Execute / Yield Stance System</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">How the Stance System Works</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>At battle start, Jiutian Xuannv begins in <span class="highlight">Yield stance</span> (执白) by default.</li>
              <li>Her passive <em>Swift Control, Slow Response</em> designates the <strong>frontmost</strong> ally as the <span class="highlight">White piece</span> (damage received reduced) and the <strong>rearmost</strong> ally as the <span class="highlight">Black piece</span> (damage dealt increased).</li>
              <li>Her Ultimate reads the current unit count: if friendly units &ge; enemies, she switches to <span class="highlight">Execute stance</span> + ATK Speed buff. If enemies outnumber friendlies, she switches to <span class="highlight">Yield stance</span> + ATK Speed buff.</li>
              <li><strong>Execute stance (执黑):</strong> Attacks the current target and builds an ATK bonus with every hit, up to a cap. Favors focused single-target ramp damage.</li>
              <li><strong>Yield stance (执白):</strong> Attacks the weakest enemy. Functions as a cleanup and pickoff tool - excellent for removing low-HP targets and exposed backline units.</li>
              <li>The White and Black piece designations can swap once per field when positional thresholds are crossed - triggering a shield based on Jiutian's ATK at Skill Lv3.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top:16px; border-color: rgba(180,130,80,0.25); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(180,130,80,0.06), rgba(180,130,80,0.04));">
            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--accent-gold-light);">Why Positioning Is Non-Negotiable</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>The White/Black piece system fires based on <em>physical position at battle start</em>. Incorrect frontline or backline slot assignments misfires the buffs - potentially giving damage reduction to a carry and damage bonus to a tank.</li>
              <li>The Ultimate's stance switch depends on live unit count - team deaths shift her mode. In a losing fight she may move to Yield (cleanup) at exactly the moment more burst pressure is needed.</li>
              <li>CN community notes this is the single most important hidden mechanic for getting full value from her. Do not auto-slot her into random positions.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SKILLS -->
        <section class="section" id="jiutian-skills">
          <div class="section-title">Skill Breakdown</div>
          <div class="skills-grid">

            <div class="skill-card ultimate">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/jiutian_xuannv_skill_1.png" alt="Win Half Against Heaven" />
                <span class="skill-name">Win Half Against Heaven</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-ultimate">Ultimate</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Reads the battlefield and switches stance based on unit count. If friendly unit count &ge; enemy unit count: switches to <span class="highlight">Execute stance</span> and grants an ATK Speed boost. If friendly unit count &lt; enemy unit count: switches to <span class="highlight">Yield stance</span> and grants an ATK Speed boost.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Deals damage to all enemy units equal to a percentage of their highest ATK.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Execute stance grants a greater ATK increase per hit.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Yield stance additionally grants a basic attack damage boost for a duration.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The Ultimate is a state manager, not a damage nuke. Cast it to set the correct stance for the current battlefield phase - Execute while winning for ramp damage; Yield while behind for cleanup. Lv2 adds an AoE damage component that partially compensates for the lack of a traditional nuke payload.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card relic">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/jiutian_xuannv_relic.png" alt="Strike the Void, Hit the Real" />
                <span class="skill-name">Strike the Void, Hit the Real</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-relic">Relic</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Strengthens both stances. <span class="highlight">Execute:</span> Each attack additionally deals bonus damage based on own ATK and the target's max HP (capped). <span class="highlight">Yield:</span> The first attacks after entering Yield stance deal bonus damage based on own ATK and the target's lost HP (capped).
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">When Enter the Game activates and hits are received, gains energy and resets the formation cooldown (proc chance).</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">The Enter the Game cooldown reset becomes guaranteed instead of chance-based.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Execute and Yield stance damage ratios and upper limits are further increased.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Lv1 is immediately impactful - bonus damage in both stances is felt right away. Lv3 is the major functional breakpoint: the Enter the Game cooldown reset shifts from probabilistic to guaranteed, making her defensive conversion loop far more reliable. CN players debate "Jiutian Relic Lv3 vs Zeus Relic Lv2" - suggesting the Lv3 upgrade is considered high-value.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/jiutian_xuannv_skill_2.png" alt="Swift Control, Slow Response" />
                <span class="skill-name">Swift Control, Slow Response</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 2</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                At battle start, designates the frontmost ally as the <span class="highlight">White piece</span> (damage received reduced) and the rearmost ally as the <span class="highlight">Black piece</span> (damage dealt increased). When White advances into enemy territory it converts to Black; when Black is approached by an enemy it converts to White. Each swap triggers once per field.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Black piece damage bonus percentage increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">When a unit swaps designation, it gains a shield based on a percentage of Jiutian's ATK.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">White piece damage reduction effect increased.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                Fires at battle start with no action required. Its entire value is positional - wrong slot assignment negates the benefit. Run a dedicated frontline tank and a dedicated backline carry to ensure the correct designations land. Lv3 adds a shield on designation swap, giving whoever repositions first a meaningful survivability layer.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/jiutian_xuannv_skill_3.png" alt="Tactical Interception" />
                <span class="skill-name">Tactical Interception</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 3</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Fires at multiple targets nearest to her, dealing ATK-based damage (hits the same target multiple times if fewer targets than projectiles). Energy comparison determines secondary effect: if target's energy is <em>below</em> Jiutian's, she <span class="highlight">recovers her own energy</span>. If target's energy is <em>equal to or above</em> hers, she <span class="highlight">drains the target's energy</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Energy recovered when target energy is below Jiutian's is further increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Energy drained when target energy is equal to or above Jiutian's is further increased.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Energy drain when target energy is equal to or above Jiutian's becomes significantly larger.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                More than raw damage - this skill adds genuine energy disruption. Against high-energy-rotation enemies (bosses, energy-cycling supports), the drain side becomes extremely valuable. The self-recovery side accelerates her own Ultimate cadence in early-fight phases. Upgrade priority increases in sustained PvE content where energy denial compounds over multiple rotations.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/jiutian_xuannv_skill_4.png" alt="Enter the Game" />
                <span class="skill-name">Enter the Game</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Skill 4</span>
              </div>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                When Jiutian Xuannv receives an attack, she summons the <span class="highlight">Taiji Formation</span>. During the formation, all incoming damage is 100% nullified and accumulated. After the formation ends, she fires at the nearest enemy dealing the accumulated total as her attack. This skill has a cooldown.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Skill cooldown slightly reduced.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Skill cooldown greatly reduced.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Continuously gains higher damage nullification during the formation.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                A defensive-to-offensive converter. She does not simply tank hits - she stores them and fires them back. Against enemies who cannot burst her down in one rotation, she generates additional damage from their own aggression. Benefits from controlled, medium-duration exchanges. Hard one-shots before the formation triggers waste this mechanic entirely.
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Skill Upgrade Priority</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>1. Win Half Against Heaven (Ultimate)</strong> - State-management core; Lv2 AoE and Lv3 Execute bonus are both meaningful upgrades</li>
              <li><strong>2. Strike the Void, Hit the Real (Relic)</strong> - Lv3 guaranteed Enter the Game reset is the single largest power spike in her kit</li>
              <li><strong>3. Tactical Interception</strong> - Energy drain at Lv4 becomes a major disruption tool in sustained PvE</li>
              <li><strong>4. Swift Control, Slow Response</strong> - Lv3 shield on designation swap adds survivability to the positional loop</li>
              <li><strong>5. Enter the Game</strong> - Cooldown reductions matter but are partially covered by Relic Lv2/3 anyway</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RATINGS -->
        <section class="section" id="jiutian-ratings">
          <div class="section-title">Mode Ratings (CN Community Assessment)</div>
          <div class="rating-grid">
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVE / Tower</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="S">S</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Clubs Tower core; reduces difficulty and scales over longer fights</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">Boss / High-Score</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="S">S</span></div>
