        <!-- STRENGTHS / WEAKNESSES -->
        <section class="section" id="jiutian-strengths">
          <div class="section-title">Strengths &amp; Weaknesses</div>
          <div class="sw-grid">
            <div class="sw-card strengths">
              <div class="sw-title">Strengths</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Flexible dual-stance system adapts to board state automatically - Execute for ramp, Yield for cleanup</li>
                <li>Energy manipulation via Tactical Interception adds genuine disruption value beyond raw damage, especially in boss and PvE content</li>
                <li>Enter the Game converts enemy aggression into counter-damage, punishing sustained multi-hit patterns</li>
                <li>Scales strongly in longer PvE fights where mode cycling, energy drain compounding, and Relic bonuses all have time to stack</li>
                <li>High relevance in Clubs Tower (梅花塔) and push content - CN community explicitly notes she reduces difficulty there</li>
                <li>Relic offers clear functional breakpoints: immediate damage at Lv1, reliable defensive loop at Lv3</li>
                <li>CN reports suggest she can exceed comparable carries in specific high-damage ranking setups</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="sw-card weaknesses">
              <div class="sw-title">Weaknesses</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Heavily position-dependent - White/Black piece designation requires intentional team construction; cannot be blind-slotted</li>
                <li>Team-dependent as a carry; CN community notes she "eats investment and teammates" as a solo carry</li>
                <li>Enter the Game is bypassed by hard one-shot burst before the Taiji Formation activates</li>
                <li>Stance switch logic is automated by unit count - in a losing fight she may enter Yield mode when Execute pressure is more needed</li>
                <li>PvP ceiling less established than PvE; CN sources focus primarily on tower and boss content</li>
                <li>Underperforms early game without proper positioning and team support in place</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SYNERGY -->
        <section class="section" id="jiutian-synergy">
          <div class="section-title">Synergy Considerations</div>
          <div class="synergy-list">
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Pan</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Cited in CN challenge guides as a mandatory partner in Jiutian's time-limited challenge stages. Pan's crowd control layers with Jiutian's energy drain to slow enemy ultimate rotations. AoE CC also gives the Taiji Formation time to cycle before enemies can focus Jiutian down.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Jormungandr</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Repeatedly featured in CN Clubs Tower team compositions alongside Jiutian. DoT damage compounds naturally with the longer fight durations Jiutian's energy manipulation and mode cycling create. Both heroes benefit from extended PvE encounters rather than short burst windows.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Nezha</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">CN community explicitly describes Jiutian and Nezha as "quite useful together." Nezha provides consistent front-loaded burst pressure that pairs with Jiutian's ranged stance-switching output - two different damage vectors operating simultaneously without competing for the same resources.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Anubis</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Present in the CN zero-spender Clubs Tower team lineup alongside Jiutian. His targeting logic and CC patterns create controlled fight conditions where Jiutian's positional designation system and stance switches function as intended.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Dedicated Frontline Tank</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Any hero filling the frontmost position reliably receives the White piece designation - damage received reduced. A proper tank absorbs the early burst that would otherwise threaten the board-presence threshold Jiutian's Ultimate relies on to stay in Execute mode.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Energy Accelerators (e.g. Caishen)</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Faster team Energy cycles mean more Ultimate casts, more stance switches, and more Tactical Interception procs per fight. Each additional Ultimate cast also creates another opportunity to set the optimal stance for the current board state.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Clubs Faction Stack</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">CN posts consistently place Jiutian in Clubs faction (梅花) teams. The faction bonus grants team-wide ATK and HP at 3-5 member thresholds - directly amplifying Execute stance ramp damage and improving survivability for Enter the Game conversion cycles.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="divider-ornament">&#10022; &#10022; &#10022;</div>

        <!-- PLAYSTYLE SUMMARY -->
        <section class="section" id="jiutian-playstyle">
          <div class="section-title">Playstyle Summary</div>
          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Jiutian Xuannv rewards players who treat her like a chess player rather than a damage dealer. Her value is not in holding a button - it is in ensuring the frontmost and rearmost slots are intentionally filled, the team runs long enough for her energy drain and stance cycling to compound, and the Ultimate is cast at the right moment to set the correct stance for the fight phase.</p>
            <p>In longer PvE content - Clubs Tower, push stages, high-damage boss rankings - this design flourishes. In short burst PvP environments the return on mechanical investment is lower. She is most rewarding for players who understand their team's positional structure and are building toward Clubs faction synergies.</p>
            <p>The honest CN verdict: strong but not idiot-proof. She is not a plug-and-play carry. She is a board-control archer whose ceiling is high and whose floor depends entirely on how well her positioning and team structure are constructed around her kit.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
    )}

