        <div class="print-bar">
          <button class="print-btn" onclick="window.print()">Save as PDF</button>
        </div>

        <!-- OVERVIEW -->
        <section class="section" id="cronus-overview">
          <div class="section-title">Overview</div>
          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Cronus is a <strong>Legendary Support</strong> of the <strong>Starglint faction</strong> whose kit is built around a single strategic archetype: <span class="highlight">Turn-Tempo Manipulation</span>. He is not a healer, not a main DPS, and not a straightforward plug-and-play unit. Instead, his entire design revolves around making enemy skill rotations slower while making his own team's rotations faster and more impactful.</p>
            <p>His kit accomplishes three things simultaneously: <strong>controlling tempo</strong> by debuffing enemy ATK Speed, cooldowns, and Energy regeneration; <strong>manipulating cooldowns</strong> to generate extra cast windows for allied carries; and <strong>saving team members</strong> from death through a time-rewind mechanic that restores a near-dead ally to their best state within the last 5 seconds.</p>
            <p>Based on kit analysis, Cronus is mechanically very likely to be strongest in <strong>PvP</strong> and in <strong>difficult push stages</strong> where fight outcomes are decided by tempo and narrow burst windows rather than raw DPS output. In pure boss damage races he is more situational. His Relic is not an optional enhancement - the Projection system is the mechanic that defines his endgame identity.</p>
            <p class="note-muted">Guide data verified against the EN in-game client (April 2026, Deity Trial). Skill descriptions and numerical values reflect Lv.4 data from the official EN localization. Ratings are mechanics-based assessments informed by 5 trial battles, not community-confirmed tier placements.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- LORE -->
        <section class="section" id="cronus-lore">
          <div class="section-title">Lore &amp; Background</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">God of Time - Greek Mythology</div>
            <p style="font-size:14px; color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:14px; line-height:1.5;">Cronus draws on the Greek mythological figure associated with time - frequently conflated with Kronos the Titan and Khronos the personification of time in later traditions. In the game, Cronus is titled God of Time and is officially described as a Starglint faction Support whose identity revolves around rewinding allies, reducing cooldowns , and summoning projections . The game channels this mythological duality into his mechanical design as a master of temporal flow on the battlefield.</p>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><em>Temporal Vortex</em> channels his dominion over time - slowing, warping, and ultimately freezing the temporal flow for his enemies</li>
              <li><em>Ferry of Time</em> represents his ability to reach across time and pull a projection of a past ally into the current moment</li>
              <li><em>Temporal Rift</em> is a tear in the fabric of space and time - used to rearrange positioning as though repositioning pieces on a board outside time</li>
              <li><em>Rewinding Remains</em> embodies his most personal power: the ability to reverse time for a single ally, restoring them to a healthier state moments before a lethal blow lands</li>
              <li><em>Echo of Causality</em> reflects cause and effect across time - when a chosen traveler acts, Cronus ensures that action reverberates a second time</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- PROJECTION SYSTEM -->
        <section class="section" id="cronus-projection">
          <div class="section-title">Core Mechanic - The Projection System</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Ferry of Time - How Projections Work</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>Cronus's Relic (<strong>Doctrine of Time</strong>) grants the skill <strong>Ferry of Time</strong>: every <strong>15 seconds</strong>, Cronus projects a Translucent Echo of an allied god into battle for <strong>6 seconds</strong>. <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic;">[Verified - EN Client]</span></li>
              <li>Projection priority: the <em>Time Traveler</em> is projected first; otherwise allies are projected from highest to lowest ATK.</li>
              <li>The projection inherits <strong>50% of Cronus's ATK and Max HP</strong> - it scales with how Cronus is built, not with the stats of the unit being projected. It copies <strong>all skills</strong> of the projected unit, and its character and skill levels scale with Cronus's level.</li>
              <li>At <strong>Relic Lv2 [Relic Lv.10]</strong>, when the Translucent Echo spawns, <strong>all skill CDs of the Echo are refreshed</strong> - enabling immediate skill output at the moment of projection arrival.</li>
              <li>At <strong>Relic Lv3 [Relic Lv.20]</strong>, projection duration is extended to <strong>10 seconds</strong>, significantly increasing the window for the copied skills to fire.</li>
              <li>At <strong>Relic Lv4</strong>, the projection spawns with <strong>1000 Energy</strong> - enabling it to fire an Ultimate almost immediately upon entering the field.</li>
              <li>The core loop: <strong>Cronus slows and disrupts enemies - Projection spawns as a copy of a key ally - Relic Lv2 refreshes Echo CDs - the team gains a second damage source within one fight window.</strong></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top:16px; border-color: rgba(180,130,80,0.25); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(180,130,80,0.06), rgba(180,130,80,0.04));">
            <div class="mechanic-label" style="color: var(--accent-gold-light);">Why Relic Investment Matters - Competitive Breakpoints</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>Relic Lv1:</strong> Projection is active (6s duration, 50% ATK/HP) - viable as a temporary allied copy, but the impact is limited without the CD refresh.</li>
              <li><strong>Relic Lv2 [Relic Lv.10]:</strong> Echo CD refresh on spawn - the first genuine power spike. This is the minimum competitive investment level.</li>
              <li><strong>Relic Lv3 [Relic Lv.20]:</strong> Duration extended to 10s - a substantial increase in the projection's active window.</li>
              <li><strong>Relic Lv4:</strong> Projection spawns with 1000 Energy - the endgame breakpoint where Cronus transitions from strong support to a tempo-multiplying carry.</li>
              <li><strong>Relic Item - Doctrine of Time</strong> (observed at Lv.18/35): HP +14.0%, ATK +11.2%, Armor +18.5%, M-RES +18.5%.</li>
              <li>Cronus's endgame identity depends on the Relic. Relic Lv2 (Lv.10) is the first competitive breakpoint. Relic Lv4 is the point where Cronus transitions from strong utility support to fight-warping tempo multiplier.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SKILLS -->
        <section class="section" id="cronus-skills">
          <div class="section-title">Skill Breakdown</div>
          <div class="skills-grid">

            <div class="skill-card ultimate">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/cronus_skill_1.png" alt="Temporal Vortex" />
                <span class="skill-name">Temporal Vortex</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-ultimate">Ultimate</span>
              </div>
              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Summons a Temporal Vortex that deals <span class="highlight">280% ATK</span> Magical DMG to all enemy units, reducing their <span class="highlight">ATK SPD by 100%</span> and <span class="highlight">Move SPD by 100%</span> for <span class="highlight">5s</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Also increases enemy active skill CD by 5 seconds for enemies within the area.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Increases DMG dealt to 360% ATK.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Affected enemies cannot regenerate Energy naturally during the effect duration.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                This is a layered anti-tempo AoE with four distinct debuff layers: damage, tempo-down, skill-delay, and energy-deny. Lv2 delays enemy active skills directly. Lv4 cuts off natural Energy regeneration entirely during the debuff window - effectively preventing enemies from reaching their next Ultimate through passive regen. The skill wins not through burst but through timing theft: it shifts enemy rotations backward and opens narrow fight windows in your favor.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card relic">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/cronus_relic.png" alt="Ferry of Time" />
                <span class="skill-name">Ferry of Time</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-relic">Relic</span>
              </div>
              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Every <span class="highlight">15 seconds</span>, Cronus cyclically projects a Translucent Echo of a teammate into the battle for <span class="highlight">6 seconds</span>. Priority: <em>Time Traveler</em> first, then allies from highest to lowest ATK. The Echo inherits <span class="highlight">50% of Cronus's ATK and Max HP</span> and copies all skills. Scales with Cronus's level.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2 [Relic Lv.10]</span><span class="upgrade-text">Upon entering the battlefield, the Translucent Echo refreshes all skill CDs.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3 [Relic Lv.20]</span><span class="upgrade-text">Translucent Echo duration is increased to 10s.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Translucent Echo gains 1000 Energy upon entering battle.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The most impactful piece of Cronus's kit. Relic Lv2 (unlocked at Relic Lv.10) is the first competitive breakpoint - the CD refresh on Echo spawn enables immediate skill output. Lv4 makes the Echo immediately dangerous by entering with 1000 Energy, enabling it to fire an Ultimate almost instantly. The 50% ATK/HP inheritance means Cronus's own stat investment directly determines the Echo's combat effectiveness.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/cronus_skill_2.png" alt="Temporal Rift" />
                <span class="skill-name">Temporal Rift</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Active</span>
              </div>
              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                Cronus teleports the nearest enemy to the position of the farthest enemy, dealing <span class="highlight">180% ATK</span> Magical DMG to both targets and <span class="highlight">Stunning</span> them for <span class="highlight">2 seconds</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Increases DMG dealt to 200% ATK.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">Each time an allied unit casts an Active Skill, the CD of this skill is reduced by 0.5 seconds.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Stun duration is increased to 3s.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                This is not a standard single-target CC - it is Formation Break plus Double-Hit Stun. Teleporting the nearest enemy to the farthest position collapses defensive spacing and exposes backline targets. Lv3 creates a self-reinforcing CD loop: the more your team casts, the faster this skill returns, generating more displacement and more Stuns.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/cronus_skill_3.png" alt="Rewinding Remains" />
                <span class="skill-name">Rewinding Remains</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Passive</span>
              </div>
              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                When an allied unit is about to fall, Cronus rewinds that unit to its <span class="highlight">optimal state from the past 5 seconds</span>. After the rewind, the target's ATK and ATK SPD are reduced by <span class="highlight">90%</span> for <span class="highlight">2s</span>. Base CD: <span class="highlight">18s</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Reduces the CD to 15s.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">When Cronus is about to fall, this effect triggers once for free on himself.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Reduces the CD to 12s.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                This is not a revive - it is a time rewind. The distinction matters: unlike resurrection mechanics, the ally does not die first. Their entire state is restored to a pre-burst snapshot, including HP, Energy, and any buffs that were active. Lv3 makes Cronus himself extremely difficult to eliminate by focus-fire, since he gains the same self-save once per fight.
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="skill-card">
              <div class="skill-header">
                <img class="skill-icon" src="https://pub-a33abfbc3135413881a1d8eb86543559.r2.dev/skills/cronus_skill_4.png" alt="Echo of Causality" />
                <span class="skill-name">Echo of Causality</span>
                <span class="skill-badge badge-skill">Passive</span>
              </div>
              <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic; display:block; margin-top:4px;">[Verified - EN Client]</span>
              <p class="skill-desc">
                At the start of battle, marks the allied unit with the highest <span class="highlight">CD Reduction</span> as <em>[Time Traveler]</em>. When the Time Traveler casts an Active Skill (excluding Ultimate and Entry Skill), <span class="highlight">that skill is cast again immediately</span>. Base CD: <span class="highlight">20s</span>.
              </p>
              <div class="skill-upgrade-block">
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv2</span><span class="upgrade-text">Reduces the skill CD to 18s.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv3</span><span class="upgrade-text">At the start of battle, reduce the initial CD of all allied units by 5s.</span></div>
                <div class="upgrade-row"><span class="skill-upgrade-level">Lv4</span><span class="upgrade-text">Reduces the skill CD to 15s.</span></div>
              </div>
              <div class="skill-note">
                The second cornerstone of Cronus's kit alongside the Projection. The Time Traveler designation targets the ally with the highest CD Reduction stat - that ally's active skill (excluding Ultimate and Entry) fires a second time immediately. The 20s base CD (15s at Lv4) means this effect fires roughly every other active rotation. Lv3 gives the entire team a faster fight start by reducing initial CDs by 5s. Build CDR on your primary carry to ensure they are consistently designated.
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top: 20px;">
            <div class="mechanic-label">Skill Upgrade Priority</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>1. Echo of Causality (Passive 2)</strong> - Pre-battle CD reduction at Lv3 creates a team-wide tempo advantage from the opening second; the double-cast on the Time Traveler is the constant engine of Cronus's value</li>
              <li><strong>2. Ferry of Time (Relic)</strong> - Lv2 CD reset on projection spawn is the first major power spike; Lv4 initial Energy is the endgame breakpoint. Minimum competitive level: Relic Lv2</li>
              <li><strong>3. Temporal Vortex (Ultimate)</strong> - Lv4 Energy block prevents enemies from naturally regenerating Energy during the debuff window, compounding the anti-tempo effect significantly</li>
              <li><strong>4. Rewinding Remains (Passive 1)</strong> - Lv3 self-save makes Cronus significantly harder to eliminate by focus-fire; upgrade after the core offensive systems are established</li>
              <li><strong>5. Temporal Rift (Active)</strong> - Lv3 CD reduction loop accelerates formation disruption frequency; strong but lower priority than the passive systems that define Cronus's identity</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- RATINGS -->
        <section class="section" id="cronus-ratings">
          <div class="section-title">Mode Ratings</div>
          <div class="rating-grid">
            <div class="rating-card">
              <div class="rating-mode">PVP</div>
              <div class="rating-cell"><span class="rating-badge" data-tier="SS">SS</span></div>
              <div class="rating-desc">Rewind save + formation break + CD manipulation + Projection = dominant in most PvP scenarios</div>
            </div>
