        <!-- NOTE SYSTEM -->
        <section class="section" id="meret-notes">
          <div class="section-title">Core Mechanic - The Note System</div>
          <div class="mechanic-box">
            <div class="mechanic-label">How Notes Are Assigned</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li><strong>Sun Note</strong> is assigned at battle start to the ally with the <strong>highest HP</strong>. This is almost always the frontline tank. The Sun Note grants a shield and increases Max HP, providing immediate frontline protection.</li>
              <li><strong>Moon Note</strong> is assigned at battle start to the ally with the <strong>highest ATK</strong>. This should be your main carry. The Moon Note increases ATK and, at Skill Lv3, also grants a Crit Rate bonus.</li>
              <li><strong>Star Note</strong> is assigned to <strong>Meret herself</strong>. It provides two Energy benefits: a passive <strong>+10% Energy regeneration</strong> from Universal Resonance, and a burst of <strong>200 Energy</strong> when the Ultimate activates. Together these significantly accelerate her Ultimate cycle.</li>
              <li>All three Notes are distributed <strong>passively at battle entry</strong> before any action is taken. Activating the Ultimate triggers all Notes to deliver their buffs simultaneously.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mechanic-label" style="margin-top: 16px;">Universal Resonance - Damage Sharing</div>
            <ul class="mechanic-list">
              <li>While Notes are active, incoming damage to any Note-bearer is split: the target takes <strong>60%</strong>, the remaining <strong>40% is divided among the other Note holders</strong>. A focused burst on your carry is reduced from 100% to 60% - significant, but not fully redistributed.</li>
              <li>This is Meret's primary anti-burst tool. Single-target elimination attempts against the main carry are significantly softened.</li>
              <li>The sharing applies regardless of who is attacked - burst aimed at the frontline is also split with the carry and Meret. All three Note-bearers contribute to absorbing damage, so their combined HP pool matters.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="mechanic-label" style="margin-top: 16px;">Critical Requirement: Stat Hierarchy</div>
            <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--text-muted); line-height:1.7;">
              Note assignment is fully automated. If a secondary DPS has higher ATK than the intended carry, Moon Note goes to the wrong unit. If a support runs higher HP than the tank, Sun Note misses the frontline. Your team needs one clear tank (highest HP) and one clear carry (highest ATK) - otherwise the Note system misfires.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="mechanic-box" style="margin-top:16px; border-color: rgba(180,130,80,0.25); background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(180,130,80,0.06), rgba(180,130,80,0.04));">
