              <div class="sw-title">Weaknesses</div>
              <ul class="sw-list">
                <li>Note targeting is fully automated - a poorly built team with unclear stat hierarchy causes Notes to land on the wrong units</li>
                <li>No direct damage output - her value depends entirely on the carry she supports</li>
                <li>Full-team AoE burst can exceed the combined Note-bearer HP pool, bypassing the damage-sharing protection</li>
                <li>If enemies target Meret directly and ignore Note-bearers, the Note system collapses</li>
                <li>Athena is the only substitute but does not replicate Meret's buff and tempo contribution</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- SYNERGY -->
        <section class="section" id="meret-synergy">
          <div class="section-title">Synergy Considerations</div>
          <div class="synergy-list">
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Heracles</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">The primary Moon Note target. Moon Note's ATK buff and Crit Rate (Lv3) feed directly into Heracles's burst output, and the Relic death-save protects him from the burst-kill attempts that typically end carry runs. The two heroes work as a pair - Meret's value scales directly with Heracles's damage ceiling.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Bastet</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">The primary Sun Note target in the Diamonds lineup. Bastet's high HP as the frontline anchor ensures Sun Note lands correctly without stat manipulation. Meret's shield and Max HP bonus on Bastet directly extend her frontline uptime, which in turn protects the burst window Heracles needs. Stable combination in both PvE and PvP content.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Phoenix</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Meret and Phoenix together create two separate survival layers for the Diamonds team. Meret handles pre-death burst mitigation through Note sharing and Relic. Phoenix handles post-death recovery through revive. The combination means a failed burst window does not end the run. Both heroes are present in the established endgame lineup.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="synergy-entry">
              <div class="synergy-hero-name">Set</div>
              <p class="synergy-body">Set's lifesteal aura and sustained utility extend fight duration, which compounds with Meret's time-dependent value. More fight time means more Note-buff uptime, more Sands in Stride heal ticks, and more The Curtain Never Falls emergency heals. Relevant in longer PvE encounters and sustained tower content.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="divider-ornament">&#10022; &#10022; &#10022;</div>

        <!-- PLAYSTYLE SUMMARY -->
        <section class="section" id="meret-playstyle">
          <div class="section-title">Playstyle Summary</div>
          <div class="overview-card">
            <p>Meret is a <em>passive system enabler</em>. Once deployed with the correct stat hierarchy, her Note distribution, damage sharing, healing, and Relic saves all fire automatically. The skill ceiling is not in execution but in <strong>team construction</strong>: one clear tank (highest HP), one clear carry (highest ATK).</p>
            <p>Relic Lv1 is the first mandatory unlock - it lets the team survive a failed burst attempt. Relic Lv2 (Lv.10) is the baseline for competitive play. Full Relic investment is relevant only after the rest of the Diamonds core (Heracles first) is already at high relic levels.</p>
            <p>Meret is not a hero for early or transitional rosters. She is a multiplier for a team that already has a burst anchor in Heracles and a stable frontline. Below that threshold, Athena is the correct substitute. Once the team needs tempo and buffs on top of survival - especially in higher-difficulty tower content - Meret completes the Diamonds endgame lineup.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
    )}

